# Text files are LF in the repository and in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says
# (it is true on the GitHub Windows runner and in a default Git for Windows install).
# The binary embeds prompts, flow definitions and templates with include_str!, and tests
# compare snapshots and recorded bodies byte for byte: a CRLF checkout would change what
# nav.exe sends to a model and break those comparisons.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Golden fixtures are compared byte for byte (SHA-256 manifest, wire bodies): never
# convert them, even on commit.
tests/fixtures/** -text
